  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"rschema_0488\" consists of four tables: Department, Employee_Table, Email_Configuration, and Employee_Maintenance_Email_Server.\nThe Department table represents the departments within the organization. It contains columns for Allow_Customer_Work_Orders (a string), Department_ID (an integer primary key), Description (a string), Disable_Auto_Reply (a boolean), Email (a string), Hide_Department (a string), Name (a string), Reply_by_Email_Only (a boolean), Request_Feedback (a string), and Sorting_Order (a string).\nThe Employee_Table table represents the employees within the organization. It contains columns for Department_ID (an integer), Employee_ID (an integer primary key), Gender (a string), Name (a string), and Phone (a string).\nThe Email_Configuration table represents the email configurations for each department. It contains columns for Configuration_ID (an integer primary key), Department_ID (an integer not null, which is a foreign key referencing the Department table), Host_Address (a string), Login_Password (a string), Login_Username (a string), and Port_Number (an integer).\nFinally, the Employee_Maintenance_Email_Server table represents the maintenance tasks for each employee on each server. It contains columns for Employee_ID (an integer not null, which is a foreign key referencing the Employee_Table table), Maintenance_Time (a datetime), and Server_ID (an integer not null, which is a foreign key referencing the Email_Configuration table). The primary key of this table is a composite of Employee_ID, Server_ID, and Maintenance_Time.",
  "gold_question": "This backend system is designed for managing work order processing information across different support departments.\n1.Department Management:The system allows you to create, modify, and delete different support departments. For each department, you can set:\nDepartment name, description, and email address.Sorting order. Whether the department only allows customers to submit work orders.Whether work orders are only responded to via email pipeline.Whether auto-replies are disabled.Whether the department is hidden from users.\n2.Email Configuration:For each department, configure the email server’s host address, port number, login username, and password, allowing the system to automatically handle emails.\n3.Employee Email Server Maintenance:\nEmployees can maintain the email server in real-time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0488.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0488\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `allow_customer_work_orders` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `disable_auto_reply` boolean DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hide_department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reply_by_email_only` boolean DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_feedback` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sorting_order` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_table` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `email_configuration` (\n  `configuration_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `host_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `port_number` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`configuration_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `email_configuration_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee_maintenance_email_server` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `server_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `server_id`, `maintenance_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_maintenance_email_server_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee_table` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_maintenance_email_server_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`server_id`) REFERENCES `email_configuration` (`configuration_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
